.TH HTTP_CHUNKED 3
.SH NAME
http_chunked \- send the body of a request as chunks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "int http_chunked(http* " h ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_chunked ()
declares that the body is sent with the chunked transfer encoding ("Transfer-Encoding: chunked"
and HTTP/1.1). The size of the body does not have to be known, so it can be produced
while the request is being sent, as the prompt of a language model or the data of a
pipe.
.P
It has to be called before the request headers are sent and before
.BR http_body (3),
or implicitly by the first
.BR http_chunk (3).
Servers that do not understand chunked requests need
.BR http_body (3)
instead.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 if there is no request, the headers are out already or it has a body of known length.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_chunk(3), http_chunk_end(3)
